  "_about": "Soft Landing prototype sounds. Pending: genny is not installed in the build container, so this spec waits here until someone renders it with python tools/render_sounds.py soft-landing after moving it up to sound-specs/. The engine is a low rocket roar, a filtered noise rumble with a slow throb, looped while the engine key is held. The descent tone is a plain triangle tone at A3 with a soft fifth above, looped; the game sets its pitch from the falling speed, so it must stay a clean, steady pitch. The pad beacon is a short, soft bell ping, mono, played faster near the pad. The fuel alarm is two soft square beeps, gentle so it never masks speech. Touchdown is a padded thud with a spring creak of the legs. A crash is a heavy crunch with a short boom. The radio click is a quick squelch before each call-out. The space ambience is a very quiet low cabin hum. The title music is a slow, sparse pad and celesta loop, kept well under speech.",
